{"beat": 4, "name": "CHAPTER 1 — WHY THE BAND IS WIDE", "text": "Why so wide, with a year of data? Because demand moves on its own. The same plan, run again with the customers arriving in a different order, finishes $65,320 apart after a year, with no price change at all. Every month on this curve carries that noise. Draw the 12 points and the line through them. Each point could sit a good way higher or lower and still be the same product in the same month. So the line can tilt, and every tilt the points allow is a different elasticity. The fit reports that as a standard error, 0.67 here, and the range you saw is the line tilting as far as the points let it. The fit won't speak at all until it has 5 months and the price has moved by at least 2%. On this catalog, 2 of the 24 products failed that bar. Their prices never moved, so there was no curve to draw. Your few-week test is below that bar for every product it touched. Not a wide answer. No answer.", "provider": "library", "words": [{"word": "Why", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.279}, {"word": "so", "start": 0.372, "end": 0.522}, {"word": "wide,", "start": 0.615, "end": 0.952}, {"word": "with", "start": 0.975, "end": 1.161}, {"word": "a", "start": 1.231, "end": 1.312}, {"word": "year", "start": 1.44, "end": 1.683}, {"word": "of", "start": 1.741, "end": 1.8}, {"word": "data?", "start": 1.858, "end": 2.368}, {"word": "Because", "start": 2.577, "end": 2.856}, {"word": "demand", "start": 2.891, "end": 3.181}, {"word": "moves", "start": 3.239, "end": 3.437}, {"word": "on", "start": 3.471, "end": 3.541}, {"word": "its", "start": 3.587, "end": 3.692}, {"word": "own.", "start": 3.75, "end": 4.145}, {"word": "The", "start": 4.47, "end": 4.598}, {"word": "same", "start": 4.667, "end": 4.957}, {"word": "plan,", "start": 5.004, "end": 5.573}, {"word": "run", "start": 5.851, "end": 6.037}, {"word": "again", "start": 6.072, "end": 6.316}, {"word": "with", "start": 6.374, "end": 6.513}, {"word": "the", "start": 6.548, "end": 6.618}, {"w